Title: HTML and Markdown List Merging and Mixing
Group: test
Shortname: foo
Level: 1
Status: LS
ED: http://example.com/foo
Abstract: Tests direct HTML/Markdown list merging and mixing HTML list items with Markdown list items.
Editor: Example Editor
Date: 1970-01-01
Markup Shorthands: markdown on, markdown-blockquotes on
Boilerplate: omit document-revision
</pre>

Explicit Wrappers {#wrappers}
=================

<ul class="wrap-ul">
	* indented one
	* indented two
</ul>

<ul class="same-indent-ul">
* same indent one
* same indent two
</ul>

<ol class="wrap-ol" start="5">
	1. step five
	2. step six
</ol>

<dl class="wrap-dl">
	: term 1
	:: def 1
	<div class="group">
		: grouped term
		:: grouped def
	</div>
	: term 2
	:: def 2
</dl>

Mixed Items in Explicit HTML Lists {#mixed-explicit}
==================================

<ul class="mixed-ul">
	<li id="ul-first">html first</li>
	* md second
	<li id="ul-third">
		html third line 1

		html third para 2
	</li>
	* md fourth
</ul>

<ul class="mixed-unclosed-ul">
	<li id="ul-unclosed-1">unclosed sibling 1
	* md sibling 2
	<li id="ul-unclosed-3">unclosed parent 3:
		* nested child 1
		* nested child 2
	* md sibling 4
</ul>

<ol class="mixed-ol">
	<li id="ol-first">first step</li>
	2. second step
	<li id="ol-third">third step
	4. fourth step
</ol>

<dl class="mixed-dl">
	<dt id="dl-t1">html term 1
	<dd>html def 1
	: md term 2
	:: md def 2
	<dt id="dl-t3">html term 3</dt>
	<dd>html def 3</dd>
	: md term 4
	:: md def 4
	<div class="mixed-group">
		<dt id="dl-gt1">grouped html term
		<dd>grouped html def
		: grouped md term
		:: grouped md def
	</div>
</dl>

Mixed Items in Bare Markdown Lists {#mixed-bare}
==================================

* bare bullet 1
<li id="bare-li">bare html bullet 2</li>
* bare bullet 3

1. bare step 1
<li id="bare-multiline">
	multiline html step 2

	second paragraph of step 2
	* nested md bullet
</li>
1. bare step 3

Separate unclosed bare list:

1. unclosed bare step 1
<li id="bare-unclosed-mid">unclosed html step 2
1. unclosed bare step 3
<li id="bare-unclosed-last">unclosed html final step

Paragraph after unclosed bare html item.

* loose md 1

<li id="bare-loose">loose html 2</li>

* loose md 3

1. outer step 1
	1. inner step 1
	<li id="inner-html-step">inner html step 2</li>
	1. inner step 3
1. outer step 2

* outer with nested html list
<li id="has-nested-ul">
<ul>
<li>inner unindented html li</li>
</ul>
</li>
* after nested html list

: bare dt 1
:: bare dd 1
<dt id="bare-dt2">html dt 2</dt>
<dd>html dd 2</dd>
<dt id="bare-dt3">unclosed dt 3
<dd>unclosed dd 3
: bare dt 4
:: bare dd 4

Nesting and Non-Merging Edge Cases {#nesting}
==================================

<ul class="outer-ul">
	* outer item 1
		* nested md item
	* outer item 2
</ul>

* md outer item 1
	<ul class="inner-html-ul">
		* inner merged item
	</ul>
* md outer item 2

<dl class="outer-dl">
	: outer term
	::
		<div class="inside-dd">
			: inner dl term
			:: inner dl def
		</div>
</dl>

<ul class="ul-with-bq">
	> * blockquote item
</ul>

<ul class="mismatched-ul">
	1. numbered inside ul
</ul>

<ol class="mismatched-ol">
	* bulleted inside ol
</ol>

<ul class="ul-with-div">
	<div>
		* bullet inside div inside ul
	</div>
</ul>

<dl class="mismatched-dl">
	* bullet inside dl
</dl>

<ul class="ul-with-dl">
	: term inside ul
	:: def inside ul
</ul>

<dl class="dl-div-mismatch">
	<div>
		* bullet inside dl div
	</div>
</dl>

Unclosed HTML Inside Markdown List Item {#unclosed-in-item}
=======================================

1. Step with unclosed dl:
	<dl class="switch">
	: case a
	:: do a
1. Next step after unclosed dl.

Paragraph after list with unclosed dl.

